{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>For.</b> [It refers to] when they come to the land, that they shall remove every idol. And He mentioned six nations, and did not hesitate to mention the smallest among them, and on its account He said \"and I will cut it off\" immediately, for the others He will drive out little by little. Or the meaning of \"and I will cut it off\" is each and every one, like בנות צעדה עלי שור (Genesis 49:22)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The lemma כי renders the Hebrew כי 'for/when'; Ibn Ezra appears to read it as a temporal particle introducing the circumstances of entering the land. The phrase צום בעת is tentatively read as 'at the time'; the reading is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:43.371555565Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}